        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "How are you guys handling distance? Clearly things happen in different places (rescuing Argent Adept in Akash'Flora, it wouldn't make sense for Wraith to throw knives at an enemy on the ground not next to the tree), and part of Tachyon's Principle of Speed is that she gets to end up anywhere in the scene, which implies that other heroes can't just jump around willy nilly.\r\n\r\nI've been using cards to represent different areas (in the tree, downtown, etc), and I'm letting my players move from one card to another adjacent card on their turn if they want. These cards are placed in relation to the heroes, by the players. ie, if someone says they're going to check out downtown, they can put the downtown card by Freedom Center. If someone else wants to check out the piers, they can choose if piers are next to downtown or next to freedom  center.\r\n\r\nWhat do you all do?",
